These are the changed files this session reviews, its partition of the files this pull request changes, each with how it changed and its added and removed line counts. Give every listed file its own pass over its diff, whatever its size or role: a test, a document, a configuration file, a deleted file, and the smaller half of a pair (an interface beside its implementation, a schema beside the code that reads it) each get one, because a defect there ships as surely as one in the main file. Account for each listed file once in `files_reviewed`, by its path exactly as listed: `reviewed` once you have read its diff, or `skipped` with the reason you did not read it. The report names every file you skip or leave out of `files_reviewed` as not reviewed, with your reason.

## Partition 2 of 3

This session reviews partition 2 of the 3 the changed files are split into: review every file in <changed-files> above in full, across every commit the scope above names. Sessions running beside this one review the files in <other-changed-files>, and the findings of all 3 are merged. The diff file the scope above names holds the changes to this partition's files only.

